Skeid becomes the single entry in front of a GPU cluster that also runs Whisper. Audio transcription has to come in through Skeid like chat does: behind client_auth (k90), routed over nodes (eligibility, admission, capacity, health), one usage event per forwarded request.

Routes (OpenAI face, behind the same client gate as /v1/chat/completions):
- POST /v1/audio/transcriptions -- multipart/form-data: file, model, language, prompt, response_format, temperature, timestamp_granularities[], stream, and whatever else the client sends
- POST /v1/audio/translations -- same handler, other upstream path

Upstream: {node.url}/audio/transcriptions resp. /audio/translations, the dialect vLLM (Whisper) and speaches (faster-whisper-server) both speak. No translation: the form goes upstream as the client sent it, only `model` is replaced by the served model when an alias tier names another one (ADR 0008). Unknown form fields and repeated ones pass through.

Upload handling:
- configurable limit, hot reloaded: `uploads: { max_bytes: N }`, default 26214400 (25 MiB, OpenAI's own limit). Over it: 413 in the OpenAI error shape, no node touched, nothing metered. The JSON routes keep Mojolicious' own limit -- nothing changes for them.
- the upload is not held twice in memory: Mojolicious spools a part above 256 KiB to a temp file; the upstream request is built from the parts already parsed (file asset reused), not from a copy of the body.
- a caller client_auth refuses must not get its upload buffered first, where the server allows that.

Streaming: form field stream=true. The upstream's SSE is relayed byte-for-byte (SSE relay, same queue/drain, client abort and cut-stream handling as chat). Three dialects exist and all pass untouched:
- OpenAI and speaches: {"type":"transcript.text.delta","delta":"..."} ... {"type":"transcript.text.done","text":"...","usage"?}; speaches ends without [DONE]
- vLLM: {"object":"transcription.chunk","choices":[{"delta":{"content":"..."}}]} ... data: [DONE]; a usage frame ({"choices":[],"usage":{prompt_tokens,completion_tokens,total_tokens}}) only when the client sends stream_include_usage=true or the server runs with --enable-force-include-usage
Skeid reads along: any frame's `usage` block is merged as on the chat stream, content_bytes counts the delta text of either dialect. Skeid does not inject stream_include_usage -- the OpenAI face never changes what the client asked for (the chat relay does not inject include_usage either).

Usage event (ADR 0004), endpoint /v1/audio/transcriptions or /v1/audio/translations:
- new optional field `audio_seconds` (nullable, like content_bytes): from usage.seconds when usage.type is "duration" (vLLM json, OpenAI whisper-1), else the top-level `duration` of a verbose_json answer (vLLM, speaches), else absent = not measured
- tokens through the existing metrics normalization when the upstream reports them (OpenAI usage.type "tokens": input_tokens/output_tokens/total_tokens; vLLM stream usage frame)
- text/srt/vtt answers are not JSON: relayed as they are, nothing to read, the event has duration_ms and status only
- stores: jsonlog writes the field, DBI gets a nullable column through the additive migration; report totals / by key / by model carry audio_seconds
- pricing per second is not modelled by Langertha::Pricing: recorded, not priced (as cached tokens were first, ADR 0013)

Done when: both routes work non-streamed and streamed against local fake upstreams in t/ (vLLM-shaped and speaches-shaped), with two nodes of the same model sharing the load, max_conns and health respected, request.start/request.finish paired on every exit path (upstream error, client abort, oversize, unkeyed node), client_auth answering 401 before anything is forwarded, existing routes and tests unchanged, prove -lr t/ green. README, CONTEXT.md, POD, skeid-protocols skill and an ADR for the relayed non-chat routes and their usage units follow.

Known gaps to leave as they are: vLLM translations and every speaches json answer report no usage at all (seconds only with response_format=verbose_json); no capability check -- a chat request naming a Whisper model is routed to the Whisper node and refused there.

